CBS News has confirmed there's been a  second deadly accident this week  involving servicemembers on a training  exercise 21 year old marine private  first class christian bautista was  killed on Sunday military officials say  Bautista died when a vehicle he was  enrolled over at a Marine Corps training  facility in Bridgeport California that  same day three army troops died at Fort  Stewart in Georgia they were sergeant  first class Brian Andrew Jenkins  corporal Thomas Cole Walker and private  first class antonio gilbert garcia they  died when their Bradley Fighting Vehicle  a vehicle like this one here rolled over  their divisions commanding general  struggled to hold back tears as he  described what happened I would like to  offer my sincere condolences to the  family members of the three soldiers  that we lost and yesterday's tragic  accident it is hard enough when you lose  one soldier but when you lose three at  one time that pain is amplified  according to a recent congressional  report there were nearly twice as many  active-duty service members killed in  accidents than in combat between 2006  and 2008 eeen
 

